@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] transfer-stream-custody-boundaries
Producer stdout MUST flow only to consumer stdin through a kernel pipe; disk
bytes never appear on helper stdout or become diagnostics. Diagnostics are
discarded with a 65536-byte cap. EOF/revocation, deadline, excessive
diagnostics or either failed child stop and reap both sides before exit. Only
two successful exits may return success. The trusted caller supplies absolute
argv, never shell text. Byte rates are bounded integers using monotonic time
with at most 65536 bytes of burst credit; throttling never delays revocation.
Progress frames carry only a fixed counter, at most once per second plus
completion; a blocked progress sink revokes. Splice accounting is transport
progress only. No setuid or capabilities.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] transfer-stream-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover the argv/env selector lattice, the credit-throttle
arithmetic and status mapping, while process-level fixtures cover exact byte
custody, locks acquired before spawn, revocation/deadline kills, diagnostics
caps and the exclusive progress frame format on inherited stdout.
